<title>UK: Italy prices 1.25 bln guilder 15-year bond, +29 bp.</title>
<headline>Italy prices 1.25 bln guilder 15-year bond, +29 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been priced, lead manager ABN AMRO Hoare Govett said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The issue will be redenominated in euros in the event of the Netherlands adopting the European Union's planned single currency.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ITALY</p>
<p> AMT   1.25 BLN DFL   COUPON     6.125     MATURITY    29.MAY.12</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.79    PAY DATE    29.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    99.19     SPREAD	+29 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    AMS/ROME  PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ITALY     HOME CTRY  ITALY     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.40	SELL CONC  1.60	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.50 PCT DSL DUE ARPIL 2010 AND</p>
<p>			    7.50 PCT DSL DUE JANUARY 2023.</p>
<p> NOTES	DEAL HAS REDENOMINATION CLAUSE IN THE EVENT OF EMU.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
